  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Victor. You're verified.\n\nI checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz. The order was due at 6:15 PM and was handed to you at 6:45 PM, so it arrived 30 minutes late.\n\nFor a delivery 16 to 44 minutes late, the policy gives account credit equal to the delivery fee. Your delivery fee on this order was $2.99, and a $2.99 late-delivery credit was already added to your account at 7:07 PM tonight. That covers the compensation for this order, so I can't add another credit for the same delay.\n\nYour account credit balance is $2.99. If you have a problem with the food or a missing item, I can check that too."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, but it was really late though. Is there anything more you can do for a 30 minute wait?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand that a 30-minute wait is frustrating, especially when you were expecting food at a set time. Unfortunately, the policy caps late-delivery compensation by how late the order was. At 30 minutes, the most we can give is the delivery-fee credit, and that's already on your account. I can't add anything more for lateness.\n\nIf anything else went wrong with the order, such as a missing item or a wrong item, tell me what happened and I'll check it. Missing or wrong item claims need to be reported within 48 hours of delivery."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, fair enough. Nothing was missing or wrong, the food was just late. I'll take the $2.99 credit, thanks."
  }
